\subsection{Dataset}

The dataset is a collection of Wikipedia articles, each of which is associated with a set of sentences from the article. The sentences are selected by a heuristic that selects sentences that are likely to be important for the article. The sentences are then annotated by crowdworkers with the following labels:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Important}: The sentence is important for the article.
    \item \textbf{Not important}: The sentence is not important for the article.

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Input:} in the florida everglades a of trees were knocked down by the storm.
\item \textbf{Output:} a storm knocked down trees in the florida everglades.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Sentence Simplification}

\subsubsection{WikiLarge}

The WikiLarge dataset is a large-scale dataset for sentence simplification. It is a collection of over 1.5 million sentence pairs, each of which is a simplified version of the other.

